CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "17f884f4-9cd3-424e-ab5c-cc1157efaa48",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T16:00:02Z",
  "ticket_id": "170b-2ac9",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "SC-0: A plugin maintainer investigating any DSO-produced commit can identify all contributing agents and the triggering skill within one git command, without opening any log file or session transcript.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where users can query commit metadata to identify agents and skills, phrased as ongoing behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-1: When attribution.enabled=true, commits produced by /dso:commit include DSO trailers appended via git interpret-trailers. Scalar trailers (Jira-Ticket, DSO-Task, DSO-Story, DSO-Epic, DSO-Review-Score) included only when non-empty; DSO-Task/Story/Epic resolved by traversing the active task's parent chain upward, emitting each level only when that ticket type exists; DSO-Review-Score read from $ARTIFACTS_DIR/reviewer-findings.json score field. Multi-value trailers (DSO-Agent, DSO-Skill, DSO-Model) emit one line per unique value accumulated since the last commit.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (commit trailer generation when a feature flag is enabled) that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-2: attribution.enabled is opt-in via dso-config.conf (default: false).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property where a configuration option has a specific default state and opt-in behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-3: For any attributed commit in a multi-agent sprint session, git log --format=\"%(trailers:key=DSO-Agent,valueonly)\" returns at least two distinct non-empty lines, one per unique agent type that contributed.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property about how git commit trailers behave after implementation, verifiable through ongoing queries"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-4: When no contributor records exist and no scalar values resolve, the commit message contains no DSO trailer lines and /dso:commit exits 0.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior and expected output that persists after implementation, phrased as an ongoing conditional property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-5: A test asserts that when attribution produces trailers, the lines before the final blank-line separator contain no strings matching ^(Jira-Ticket|DSO-[A-Za-z-]+): \u2014 only the trailer block following the separator does. Commits with no body (subject-only) also satisfy this constraint.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable constraint that the system must continuously satisfy about trailer formatting behavior, even though it's expressed through a test assertion"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-6: After git commit exits 0, $ARTIFACTS_DIR/attribution-contributors.jsonl exists and has size 0. If truncation fails, /dso:commit emits a warning to stderr but does not fail.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior and properties that persist after the work (file existence, size, warning emission on failure) rather than a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC-7: When git <2.6 is detected, TRAILER_SKIPPED is emitted to stderr, attribution is skipped, and /dso:commit continues. A test verifies this by injecting a mock git version string below 2.6 and asserting TRAILER_SKIPPED on stderr with no DSO trailer lines in the commit message.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (git version detection and error handling) that persists after implementation, though the test itself is transitional"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
